before:
A taller float pushes the cleared paragraph farther down; the parent still encloses both.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.story { display: flow-root; width: 260px; } .thumb { float: left; width: 80px; height: 140px; margin-right: 12px; } .story p { margin: 0; } .next { clear: left; }
```

after:
The map has the class `thumb`, inside the `story` article.

```css
.story {
  display: flow-root;
  width: 260px;
}
.thumb {
  float: left;
  width: 80px;
  height: 100px;
  margin-right: 12px;
}
.story p {
  margin: 0;
}
.next {
  clear: left;
}
```

The map floats left. Its right margin leaves 12 pixels before the nearby text.
